1
00:06:33,333 --> 00:06:39,333
Together till the end

2
00:13:06,666 --> 00:13:12,666
Kursk is a drama, history, thriller film directed by Thomas Vinterberg.

3
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Barents Sea, August 12th, 2000.

4
00:26:13,333 --> 00:26:19,333
During a Russian naval exercise, and after suffering a serious accident, the
K-141 Kursk submarine sinks with 118 crew members on board.

5
00:32:46,666 --> 00:32:52,666
While the few sailors who are still alive barely manage to survive, their families push for accurate information and a
British officer struggles to obtain from the Russian government a permit to attempt a rescue before it is late.

6
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:26,000
But general incompetence are against all their efforts.

7
00:45:53,333 --> 00:45:59,333
Mikhail Averin, played by Matthias Schoenaerts.

8
00:52:26,666 --> 00:52:32,666
Tanya Averina, played by Léa Seydoux.

9
00:59:00,000 --> 00:59:06,000
Admiral Vyacheslav Grudzinsky, played by Peter Simonischek.

10
01:05:33,333 --> 01:05:39,333
Admiral Vladimir Petrenko, played by Max von Sydow.

11
01:12:06,666 --> 01:12:12,666
Anton Markov, played by August Diehl.

12
01:18:40,000 --> 01:18:46,000
Commodore David Russell, played by Colin Firth.

13
01:25:13,333 --> 01:25:19,333
Kursk (UK: Kursk: The Last Mission, US: The Command) is a 2018 disaster drama-thriller film directed by Thomas
Vinterberg, based on Robert Moore's book A Time to Die, about the true story of the 2000 Kursk submarine disaster.

14
01:31:46,666 --> 01:31:52,666
It stars Matthias Schoenaerts, Léa Seydoux, Peter Simonischek,
August Diehl, Max von Sydow, and Colin Firth.

15
01:38:20,000 --> 01:38:26,000
It was the last of von Sydow's films to be released during his lifetime.

16
01:44:53,333 --> 01:44:59,333
The film explores themes of submarine, based on true story,
struggle for survival, russian politics, russian history.

17
01:51:26,666 --> 01:51:32,666
The tone is emotional and intense.
